  "id": "COMPOUND:43609 - PROTEIN:4923",
  "verbalization": "Eurostoside is implicated in the interaction with Neuropilin-2 through a series of molecular pathways. The evidence suggests that Eurostoside acts as a target for Lysine-specific demethylase 2A, which in turn is targeted by dicloxacillin and another compound, (1S,2S,5S,8R,11S,12R)-5-hydroxy-2,12-dimethyl-6-methylidene-16-oxapentacyclo[10.3.2.15,8.01,11.02,8]octadecane-7,17-dione. These compounds are all linked to Neuropilin-2 as their targets. The varying scores across the paths indicate a consistent but not absolute relationship, with the highest confidence in the direct interaction between Eurostoside and Neuropilin-2 through Lysine-specific demethylase 2A. The evidence supports a mechanistic link where Eurostoside may influence Neuropilin-2 through the modulation of demethylase activity, potentially affecting downstream signaling pathways. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Eurostoside in modulating Neuropilin-2 function, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact mechanism and the extent of the interaction.",
